67:["$","$L3",null,{"children":["$","section",null,{"className":"border-t border-border pt-8 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"label-mono flex items-center gap-3 text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent-blue","children":"05"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"h-px w-6 bg-border"}],"Implementation"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","p","0",{"children":"The architecture is a pipeline: check → capture → evaluate → report. Each stage is independent, which keeps the core honest — the check stage can run without reporting, and reporting can be extended without touching capture. Provider-based notification means Telegram and GitHub are implementations of one notifier interface, not hardwired paths."}],["$","p","1",{"children":"Browser automation runs real page loads with explicit timeouts and retries, because flaky automation that cries wolf destroys trust in the reports. Captures are treated as evidence attached to a verdict, not as the verdict itself."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5","children":[["$","span","Python",{"className":"inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-border px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] leading-5 text-muted-foreground","children":"Python"}],["$","span","Browser Automation",{"className":"inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-border px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] leading-5 text-muted-foreground","children":"Browser Automation"}],["$","span","Telegram Bot API",{"className":"inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-border px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] leading-5 text-muted-foreground","children":"Telegram Bot API"}],["$","span","GitHub API",{"className":"inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-border px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] leading-5 text-muted-foregro